# Integrity

Do not tune on the test set. The probe split is the gate's only acceptance signal.

Record every analytical finding and every visual finding before the session ends.

Analytical record, in the ledger: step metrics, diagnostics, every edit proposal, every gate decision (accepted and rejected), lineage, and a `findings` row. Kinds are `observation`, `negative`, `claim`, and `method`. Failed seeds and negative results stay. Also write the narrative in `docs/09_JOURNAL.md`.

Visual record, during the work and not only at the end: every milestone notebook shows the process in Plotly as it happens. Before and after an edit, the gate decision, the loss or accuracy trace, and the network changing over steps are figures, not printouts. matplotlib or seaborn, Okabe-Ito, is the paper copy of the same view. Each paper figure is exported by a notebook cell with a provenance manifest (git commit, config hash, seeds, ledger version, ledger hashes, device). The finding row's `evidence_ref` points at that manifest. Title synthetic figures `SYNTHETIC`. `assert_citable` rejects them.

A claim in docs or in `paper/` names a manifest whose `synthetic` field is false. A number with no manifest is not a result. If a figure or number is worth the paper, write the ledger finding and the provenance manifest in the same session. Copy only `claim` figures into `paper/figures/`. Method checks stay in `results/` with their manifest.

Citations are sources opened in this session. If the PDF was not opened, say so and leave it off `paper/refs.bib`.

`assert_same_machine` before any pooled table. CUDA and MPS results stay in separate tables.

Hypotheses live in `docs/01_RESEARCH_QUESTIONS.md`. Edit them only with an ADR written before the confirmatory run.
